# =============================================================================
# CloudBox — declarative inventory of UPSTREAM sources for every version pin.
#
# scripts/check-consistency.sh answers "do our files agree with each other?".
# This file answers the other half: "has any pin fallen BEHIND upstream?" —
# read by scripts/check-upstream.sh (a MAINTAINER tool; it needs internet and
# is never part of the attendee flow).
#
# It deliberately contains NO version numbers: every row says where the pin
# currently lives, so versions.env / mise.toml / images.txt stay the single
# source of truth (principle 14).
#
# Format — one row per tracked artifact, fields separated by "|":
#
#   name | latest-kind | latest-locator | pin-source | track
#
#   name            short kebab-case id, unique
#
#   latest-kind     github-release  GitHub /releases/latest for <owner>/<repo>.
#                                   With a `track` it lists /releases instead
#                                   (up to 3 pages) and picks the highest
#                                   matching version.
#                   github-tag      list /tags (up to 3 pages), highest semver.
#                                   Use where upstream mismarks prereleases as
#                                   "latest" (kagent) or publishes no releases.
#                   helm-index      locator is <repo-url>#<chart-name>; reads
#                                   <repo-url>/index.yaml.
#                   registry-tag    locator is an image repo; `crane ls`.
#
#   pin-source      env:VAR                   variable in scripts/versions.env
#                   mise:<tool-key>           [tools] key in mise.toml
#                   image:<repo>              tag pinned for that repo in
#                                             scripts/images.txt (digest stripped)
#                   chart:<path>#<chart>      `helm.sh/chart: <chart>-<version>`
#                                             label in a rendered manifest
#                   file:<path>#<sed-regex>   escape hatch, one capture group.
#                                             The regex may not contain "|" or
#                                             "#" (field separators).
#
#   track           empty or "*" = any newer version counts as drift.
#                   Otherwise an extended regex matched against the upstream
#                   version with a leading "v" stripped — used for deliberate
#                   holds (CNPG 1.28.x) and for filtering prereleases out of
#                   tag/index listings. Document every hold in a comment above
#                   the row.
#
# Comment lines start with "#"; blank lines are ignored.
# =============================================================================

# --- Tooling (mise.toml + versions.env + the CI-pinned linters) --------------
mise                     | github-release | jdx/mise                                        | env:MISE_VERSION                             |
talos                    | github-release | siderolabs/talos                                | env:TALOS_VERSION                            |
helm                     | github-release | helm/helm                                       | mise:helm                                    |
kind                     | github-release | kubernetes-sigs/kind                            | mise:kind                                    |
kind-node-image          | registry-tag   | docker.io/kindest/node                          | image:docker.io/kindest/node                 |
crane                    | github-release | google/go-containerregistry                     | mise:crane                                   |
cilium-cli               | github-release | cilium/cilium-cli                               | mise:aqua:cilium/cilium-cli                  |
jq                       | github-release | jqlang/jq                                       | mise:jq                                      |
registry                 | registry-tag   | docker.io/library/registry                      | image:docker.io/library/registry             |
kubeconform              | github-release | yannh/kubeconform                               | file:.github/workflows/ci.yaml#KUBECONFORM_VERSION:[[:space:]]*(v[0-9][^[:space:]]*) |

# --- Platform: cluster + GitOps core -----------------------------------------
# The Cilium chart index carries -pre/-rc entries; only stable releases count.
cilium-chart             | helm-index     | https://helm.cilium.io#cilium                   | env:CILIUM_VERSION                           | ^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
gitea-chart              | helm-index     | https://dl.gitea.com/charts/#gitea              | env:GITEA_CHART_VERSION                      |
argocd                   | github-release | argoproj/argo-cd                                | env:ARGOCD_VERSION                           |
local-path-provisioner   | github-release | rancher/local-path-provisioner                  | env:LOCAL_PATH_PROVISIONER_VERSION           |

# --- Platform: data services -------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATE HOLD: CNPG is pinned to the mature 1.28.x minor (see
# gitops/components/cnpg-operator/VENDOR.md) — 1.29/1.30 exist and are ignored
# on purpose; this row only reports newer 1.28 patches.
# Reads TAGS, not releases: GitHub's /releases LIST endpoint returns an empty
# array for this repo (while /releases/latest happily answers v1.30.0), so the
# release-based path reported a bogus "no releases matching track". Tags are
# reliable here. That makes four rows on github-tag for the same reason —
# envoy, kagent, victoria-metrics and now this one.
cnpg                     | github-tag     | cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg                   | image:ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg  | ^1\.28\.
rustfs-chart             | helm-index     | https://charts.rustfs.com#rustfs                | chart:gitops/components/rustfs/rustfs.yaml#rustfs |
# RustFS is beta by design (RESEARCH.md §2) — prereleases are in scope here.
rustfs-image             | registry-tag   | docker.io/rustfs/rustfs                         | image:docker.io/rustfs/rustfs                |
zot                      | github-release | project-zot/zot                                 | image:ghcr.io/project-zot/zot                |
zot-chart                | helm-index     | https://zotregistry.dev/helm-charts#zot         | chart:gitops/components/zot/zot.yaml#zot     |

# --- Platform: self-service, serverless, builds, messaging -------------------
# The "stable" channel index still carries -rc entries, so track stable only —
# without this the weekly report recommended 2.4.0-rc.1 over 2.3.4.
crossplane-chart         | helm-index     | https://charts.crossplane.io/stable#crossplane  | chart:gitops/components/crossplane/crossplane.yaml#crossplane | ^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
knative-serving          | github-release | knative/serving                                 | file:gitops/components/knative-serving/serving-core.yaml#app.kubernetes.io/version: "([0-9][^"]*)" |
knative-eventing         | github-release | knative/eventing                                | env:KNATIVE_EVENTING_VERSION                 |
# Envoy backports patches to old minors, so /releases/latest can point BACKWARDS;
# read the tag list and take the highest stable instead.
# DELIBERATE HOLD on the 1.37 minor: we do not track Envoy for its own sake — we
# freeze the exact patch that net-kourier floats as `v1.37-latest` in the
# kourier.yaml we vendor. net-kourier ships `v1.37-latest` for both knative-v1.22.1
# and knative-v1.23.0, so 1.37 is the only Envoy line Kourier is tested against;
# taking 1.38/1.39 would run the Kourier data plane on an untested minor for a
# cosmetic drift row. Widen this regex when net-kourier itself moves off v1.37.
envoy                    | github-tag     | envoyproxy/envoy                                | image:docker.io/envoyproxy/envoy             | ^1\.37\.
argo-workflows           | github-release | argoproj/argo-workflows                         | image:quay.io/argoproj/workflow-controller   |
buildkit                 | github-release | moby/buildkit                                   | image:docker.io/moby/buildkit                |
nats                     | github-release | nats-io/nats-server                             | image:docker.io/library/nats                 |
prometheus-nats-exporter | github-release | nats-io/prometheus-nats-exporter                | image:docker.io/natsio/prometheus-nats-exporter |

# --- Day-2 AI agent ----------------------------------------------------------
# kagent does not mark v0.10.0-beta*/rc* tags as prereleases, so /releases/latest
# resolves to a beta (see versions.env). Read tags, stable-only.
kagent                   | github-tag     | kagent-dev/kagent                               | env:KAGENT_VERSION                           | ^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$

# --- Observability (Victoria stack + OTel Collector) -------------------------
# VictoriaMetrics publishes several release lines on the SAME DAY (1.149.0,
# 1.148.1 and LTS 1.136.15 all on 2026-08-05), and GitHub's /releases/latest
# returned the LTS patch — so this row read `ok` only because our pin happened
# to be ahead of it, and a real 1.150.0 could have gone unreported. Read the
# tag list and take the highest stable instead. The sibling VictoriaLogs and
# VictoriaTraces repos each have a single line, so they stay on github-release.
# That change paid off on 2026-08-17: 1.150.0 shipped and this row reported it
# as `minor` — /releases/latest was still pointing at an LTS patch.
victoria-metrics         | github-tag     | VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics                 | image:docker.io/victoriametrics/victoria-metrics | ^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
victoria-logs            | github-release | VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs                    | image:docker.io/victoriametrics/victoria-logs |
victoria-traces          | github-release | VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaTraces                  | image:docker.io/victoriametrics/victoria-traces |
# Stock Grafana is not in images.txt: it is only the FROM line of
# apps/grafana/Dockerfile (a build input for ghcr.io/randax/cloudbox-grafana),
# so the pin is read straight out of that Dockerfile.
grafana                  | github-release | grafana/grafana                                 | file:apps/grafana/Dockerfile#FROM grafana/grafana:([0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+) |
otel-collector-contrib   | github-release | open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-releases | image:docker.io/otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib |

# --- Lab workload images -----------------------------------------------------
# aws/aws-cli publishes no GitHub releases, and the repo still carries v1 tags.
aws-cli                  | github-tag     | aws/aws-cli                                     | image:public.ecr.aws/aws-cli/aws-cli         | ^2\.

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT tracked — DERIVED from something that IS tracked above, or
# not expressible as a version comparison. Bump these by re-vendoring their
# parent, never on their own.
#
#   Talos release (`talosctl images default`)
#     KUBERNETES_VERSION in versions.env, and with it mise.toml's kubectl pin.
#     This is the row that most looks like it belongs above and does not: the
#     number is not ours to choose. create-cluster.sh passes it as
#     --kubernetes-version, so it must be exactly what `talosctl images default`
#     reports for TALOS_VERSION. Tracking kubernetes/kubernetes here would report
#     drift on every upstream patch and invite raising it on its own — which pulls
#     four control-plane images that are not in the mirror while every other check
#     stays green (they exist upstream; mise.toml bumps in lockstep). The
#     constraint is enforced instead of reported: check-consistency.sh asserts
#     that images.txt carries kubelet + kube-{apiserver,controller-manager,
#     scheduler} at exactly v${KUBERNETES_VERSION}, so a lone bump fails CI.
#     Bump it by re-deriving from Talos, never by reading a Kubernetes release.
#     ghcr.io/siderolabs/kubelet, registry.k8s.io/kube-{apiserver,controller-
#     manager,scheduler}, etcd, coredns/coredns, pause,
#     networking/kube-network-policies
#   Cilium chart
#     quay.io/cilium/{cilium,operator-generic,cilium-envoy} (digest-pinned by
#     `helm template`)
#   Gitea chart
#     docker.gitea.com/gitea (the chart's appVersion)
#   ArgoCD release manifest
#     ghcr.io/dexidp/dex, public.ecr.aws/docker/library/redis
#   CNPG release
#     ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/postgresql (default image compiled into the
#     operator; the Backstage database pins the same tag)
#   local-path-provisioner manifest
#     docker.io/library/busybox (helper pod image)
#   knative releases
#     every gcr.io/knative-releases/... digest (serving, eventing, kourier) —
#     they come out of the vendored release YAMLs
#   kagent chart
#     ghcr.io/kagent-dev/kagent/{tools,ui,app,skills-init},
#     docker.io/library/postgres:18.3-alpine (chart default)
#
#   docker.io/library/postgres:18-alpine — module 05's fault lab pins the
#     floating minor tag on purpose (the scenario needs "a postgres", not a
#     specific patch).
#   ghcr.io/knative/helloworld-go — upstream publishes only :latest, so we pin
#     a digest; there is no version to compare.
#   ghcr.io/cnoe-io/backstage-app — pinned to a CNOE git SHA
#     (gitops/components/backstage/VENDOR.md), not a semver tag. Re-verify by
#     hand against cnoe-io/stacks `ref-implementation/backstage`.
#   ghcr.io/randax/cloudbox-{portal,uploader,resizer,grafana} — first-party,
#     built from apps/ by .github/workflows/build-images.yaml.
#   mise.toml node = "24" — major-pinned on purpose (Slidev only); any 24.x is
#     acceptable, so "behind" is meaningless.
#   docker.io/library/busybox:1.37.00 (lab/05 fault injection) — deliberately
#     broken, never bumped.
# =============================================================================
